1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,589
What was your expectation before coming to greece and how did it live up to that.
来希腊之前你有怎样的期待？实际情况和期待比起来怎么样？

2
00:00:04,599 --> 00:00:12,599
Before I came to greece my only prior knowledge to it was from the movies like mama m or my big fat greek wedding if you've seen those before.
来之前，我只从电影里了解希腊，比如字幕写作 mama m 的电影，还有《我的盛大希腊婚礼》，不知道你有没有看过。

3
00:00:12,599 --> 00:00:21,239
Honestly like the islands have exceeded my expectations but coming to athens it was very different seeing the acropolis it's like it's falling apart.
说实话，海岛超出预期，但雅典很不一样。看到卫城时，感觉它好像在坍塌。

4
00:00:21,239 --> 00:00:23,879
It's not what it looks like in like the history books you know.
不像历史书里看到的样子，你知道吧。

5
00:00:23,879 --> 00:00:28,599
Back then greece was in chist so whenever I told to my friends that I'm going to gre.
那时希腊处于字幕写作 chist 的状态，我告诉朋友，我要去字幕写作 gre 的地方。

6
00:00:28,599 --> 00:00:33,390
Well well they are in crisis why do you go there like you can find a job here then you can live better.
朋友就说，他们在危机中，为什么去？在这里能找工作，过得更好。

7
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:39,840
So my expectation was uh very low but actually I can say that greece exceeded my expectations.
所以我期待很低，但事实上，希腊超出了我的期待。

8
00:00:39,840 --> 00:00:49,440
I've been here quite a few times because I'm half greek so I come every summer so my expectations have always been high because it's greece and so far honestly they're meeting them.
因为我有一半希腊血统，每年夏天都来，来过好多次，所以期待一直很高，到现在确实都达到了。

9
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:52,440
I love greece I feel like there's a different energy here.
我爱希腊，感觉这里有种不同的活力。

10
00:00:52,440 --> 00:00:57,480
What are some culture shocks you experienced upon driving positive or negative both.
你经历过什么文化冲击，正面的还是负面的？两种都说。

11
00:00:57,480 --> 00:01:05,959
So the positive things are definitely the hospitality it's top notch I'm really impressed on how friendly how kind with what a smile the greeks welcome you.
正面的肯定是待客之道，特别棒。我很惊讶，他们如此友好、亲切，带着笑容欢迎你。

12
00:01:05,959 --> 00:01:09,000
And it's not fake it's really like from the deepest of their heart.
而且不是装的，真的发自内心。

13
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:17,039
Negative things are definitely being on time if you make uh plans with people they they cancel they uh have other things to do they forget.
负面的是守时。你约好计划，他们会取消、有其他事，或者忘记了。

14
00:01:17,039 --> 00:01:23,720
But um I try to adapt because I like that the people are pretty spontaneous sometimes you make plans for let's have a coffee in a week.
但我会适应，因为我也喜欢大家挺随性。有时约好一周后喝咖啡。

15
00:01:23,720 --> 00:01:30,399
And then you feel you don't feel good or you have a tired day or the night was short or whatever some things can always happen this is life.
结果你不舒服，或很累、没睡够，反正总会有事发生，这就是生活。

16
00:01:30,399 --> 00:01:38,720
I like that the people are kind of going with the flow it's not so you have to really stick to this appointment because two weeks ago you said you're going to have coffee at that day.
我喜欢大家顺其自然，不会因为两周前约过，就非得严格按那天的约定喝咖啡。

17
00:01:38,720 --> 00:01:46,920
I guess the lack of cancel culture perhaps the lack of care when it comes to getting things done at a certain time or a certain pace.
我想也许是缺少字幕说的 cancel culture，或者不太在意在特定时间、按特定速度把事情做完。

18
00:01:46,920 --> 00:01:52,640
From toronto where I'm from it's very easy to tell somebody hey if you don't get this done there are going to be repercussions.
在我来自的多伦多，很容易对别人说：这件事不做完，就会有后果。

19
00:01:52,640 --> 00:02:00,039
If you say this to a greek here they will laugh at your face and close the door and say see you tomorrow because my working hours are done they're over.
在这里对希腊人这么说，他们会笑着关门说：明天见，我的工作时间结束了。

20
00:02:00,039 --> 00:02:13,000
I'm from philadelphia and city life is very different than greek life there's a thing called greek time where if a greek says a certain time that they'll arrive just expected to be 2 hours later.
我来自费城，城市生活和希腊生活很不一样。有个说法叫希腊时间，对方说几点来，就预期晚两个小时吧。

21
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:20,720
The slow pace of living oh that was so hard for me cuz like I come from the city I want things to be quick I want things to be done.
慢节奏生活对我可太难适应了，因为我来自城市，希望事情快点、赶紧完成。

22
00:02:20,720 --> 00:02:23,480
But greeks love to take their time they love to be present.
但希腊人喜欢慢慢来，喜欢活在当下。

23
00:02:23,480 --> 00:02:30,480
I feel like in melbour my city things open very early in the morning cafes close pretty early at 4 or 5.
我觉得在我的城市、字幕写作 melbour 的地方，店早上开得很早，咖啡馆下午四五点就关了。

24
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:35,879
And I don't understand where people find time to get coffee cuz people work I think it's more on your break from work.
我不明白大家什么时候有空喝咖啡，因为还得工作。我想大概是工作休息时。

25
00:02:35,879 --> 00:02:43,679
But in greece cafes and a lot of shops are open very late getting a coffee is something you do in the afternoon and at night and I really like this I think.
但在希腊，咖啡馆和很多店开到很晚，下午或晚上都能喝咖啡，我很喜欢。

26
00:02:43,679 --> 00:02:54,120
There's a bigger nighttime culture shops are open later you can go shopping not just bars and clubs it's normal to ask someone out for a drink at 11 00 p m.
我觉得夜间文化更丰富，商店关得晚，除了酒吧夜店还能购物，晚上十一点约喝一杯也正常。

27
00:02:54,120 --> 00:02:59,680
But in melbourne if you go go out for a drink in australia usually it'll be like right after work for me it's the opposite.
但在墨尔本、澳大利亚，出去喝一杯通常是刚下班。对我却恰好相反。

28
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:08,280
Because in argentina we used to hang out later dinner at 9 maybe is early for us we are very similar with all the mediterranean countries.
因为在阿根廷我们习惯更晚出门，九点晚餐可能还算早。我们和地中海国家很相似。

29
00:03:08,280 --> 00:03:13,800
In toronto everybody's very kind of considerate of their space and their kind of bubble.
在多伦多，每个人都挺顾及彼此的空间和个人小天地。

30
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:17,919
And here for sure one of the things that was a little bit crazy to me is the first time that I went on the metro.
这里让我有点震惊的一件事，是第一次坐地铁。

31
00:03:17,919 --> 00:03:22,680
And it was definitely rush hour because we were like a bunch of you know fish in a tin can.
那肯定是高峰期，因为我们挤得像罐头里的鱼。

32
00:03:22,680 --> 00:03:28,400
And everybody was like kind of helping each other stand up and like somebody was falling over and they would like help them over.
大家互相帮忙站稳，有人快摔倒，别人就扶一把。

33
00:03:28,400 --> 00:03:34,960
And for me if you were to do that in toronto on subway everybody would like start yelling why are you touching me and start running around and acting crazy.
对我来说，在多伦多地铁上这样做，别人可能会大叫为什么碰我，然后乱跑、情绪激动。

34
00:03:34,960 --> 00:03:41,960
Everybody here was extremely extremely helpful and I think that was definitely like a big wow for me but in a in a good way.
这里的人特别特别热心，我觉得真的让我大吃一惊，不过是好的那种。
